\pard\sa180\sb240\keepn\b\f1\fs28 1. Import pipeline throughput\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Marcus reported the nightly import now takes 42 minutes, up from 19 in April. The growth is in the validation stage, not the transfer. Batching by 500 in a spike branch brought it back to 24 minutes, but nobody could explain the memory profile.\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\i Decision: merge the batching change behind IMPORT_BATCH_SIZE, default off, and measure for a week before flipping it.\par
\pard\sa180\sb240\keepn\b\f1\fs28 2. Mobile release cut\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Priya asked to move the cut from Thursday to Monday. Two regressions in the offline queue are still open, and one has no reproduction. Dana pushed back on cutting with an unreproduced bug in the queue.\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\i Decision: hold the Thursday date, review on Wednesday morning.\par
\pard\sa180\sb240\keepn\b\f1\fs28 3. Documents upload feature\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Ines walked through the upload states: idle, uploading, converting, done, and three failure states. The converting state has no design for files above the size limit, which the gateway rejects before the client ever sees the file.\par
